issues.corrective_action:
Choose one of two options.

**(a) Preferred.** Thanks to the t component, f_hat > 0 everywhere, so the domain cut is unnecessary for LS scores:
- score every target by -f_hat(y|x) on the real line;
- for interval methods, do not clip coverage at D;
- when q_k = +inf, count the stratum as fully covered, as in (4). Report the size of such strata separately (they are unbounded), or keep the D-restricted size but state that it is a display convention.

**(b) Keep the D-restricted sets.** Then amend Section 4.4 and the Theorem 1 discussion to the correct bound Cov_k >= 1 - alpha_k - P(Y not in D | Y in B_k). Report the per-dataset, per-stratum out-of-domain fraction, and drop the sentence that Theorem 1 applies to the reported coverage.

In both cases:
- count infinite thresholds caused by +inf scores in n_strata_inf;
- add a unit test with targets outside D in a stratum with r_k > n_k.
